":"cērntu","gloss":"having reached"}],"gloss":"having reached"},{"surface":"அல்கிய","parts":[{"text":"அல்கிய","lemma":"alkiya","gloss":"that stayed"}],"gloss":"that stayed"},{"surface":"அழுங்கல்","parts":[{"text":"அழுங்கல்","lemma":"aluṅkal","gloss":"bustling"}],"gloss":"bustling"},{"surface":"ஆலை","parts":[{"text":"ஆலை","lemma":"ālai","gloss":"shed"}],"gloss":"shed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"வெளில்","parts":[{"text":"வெளில்","lemma":"veḷil","gloss":"tethering post"}],"gloss":"tethering post"},{"surface":"பாழ்","parts":[{"text":"பாழ்","lemma":"pāḻ","gloss":"desolation"}],"gloss":"desolate"},{"surface":"ஆக","parts":[{"text":"ஆக","lemma":"āka","gloss":"to become"}],"gloss":"becoming"},{"surface":"கண்டு","parts":[{"text":"கண்டு","lemma":"kaṇṭu","gloss":"having seen"}],"gloss":"having seen"},{"surface":"கலுழ்ந்து","parts":[{"text":"கலுழ்ந்து","lemma":"kaluḻntu","gloss":"having wept"}],"gloss":"having wept"},{"surface":"ஆங்கு","parts":[{"text":"ஆங்கு","lemma":"āṅku","gloss":"like"}],"gloss":"like"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"கலங்கினேன்","parts":[{"text":"கலங்கினேன்","lemma":"kalaṅkiṉēṉ","gloss":"I was distressed"}],"gloss":"I was distressed"},{"surface":"அல்லனோ","parts":[{"text":"அல்லன்","lemma":"allaṉ","gloss":"am I not"},{"text":"ஓ","lemma":"ō","gloss":"interrogative particle"}],"gloss":"am I not"},{"surface":"யானே","parts":[{"text":"யான்","lemma":"yāṉ","gloss":"I"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed I"},{"surface":"பொலம்","parts":[{"text":"பொலம்","lemma":"polam","gloss":"gold"}],"gloss":"gold"},{"surface":"தார்","parts":[{"text":"தார்","lemma":"tār","gloss":"garland"}],"gloss":"garland"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தேர்","parts":[{"text":"தேர்","lemma":"tēr","gloss":"chariot"}],"gloss":"chariot"},{"surface":"வண்","parts":[{"text":"வண்","lemma":"வண்","gloss":"generous"}],"gloss":"generous","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"கிள்ளி","parts":[{"text":"கிள்ளி","lemma":"kiḷḷi","gloss":"Killi"}],"gloss":"Killi"},{"surface":"போகிய","parts":[{"text":"போகிய","lemma":"pōkiya","gloss":"who has departed"}],"gloss":"who has departed"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பேரிசை","parts":[{"text":"பேரிசை","lemma":"pēricai","gloss":"great fame"}],"gloss":"greatly famous"},{"surface":"மூதூர்","parts":[{"text":"மூதூர்","lemma":"mūtūr","gloss":"ancient town"}],"gloss":"ancient town"},{"surface":"மன்றம்","parts":[{"text":"மன்றம்","lemma":"maṉṟam","gloss":"assembly ground"}],"gloss":"assembly ground"},{"surface":"கண்டே","parts":[{"text":"கண்டு","lemma":"kaṇṭu","gloss":"having seen"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"having seen indeed"}]}],"literal":"Abundant food having yielded, for many years having protected, / the great male elephant having lost, the distressed mahout, / that having reached, stayed in the bustling shed, / the tethering post becoming desolate, having seen, like weeping, / did I not tremble, indeed, I? With golden garland, / chariot-generous Killi who has departed, / having seen the assembly ground of the greatly famous ancient town!","translation":"Am I not shaken, just like a distressed mahout who, having lost the great elephant he had protected for many years by feeding it abundant food, weeps upon seeing the empty tethering post in the bustling shed where the elephant used to stay? Indeed, I trembled upon seeing the assembly ground of the ancient, highly renowned town, now that Killi, generous with his chariots and adorned with a golden garland, has departed.","modern":"பல ஆண்டுகள் பெருமளவு உணவு கொடுத்துக் காப்பாற்றிய தன் பெரிய ஆண் யானையை இழந்த வருத்தமுடைய பாகன், அந்த யானை தங்கியிருந்த ஆரவாரமிக்க கொட்டிலில் அதன் கட்டும் தறி பாழாய்க் கிடப்பதைக் கண்டு அழுது கலங்குவது போல, பொன்னாலான மாலையையும் தேர்க்கொடையும் உடைய கிள்ளி இறந்துபோன பிறகு, அவனது புகழ்பெற்ற பழமையான ஊரின் மன்றத்தைக் கண்டு நானும் கலங்கினேன் அல்லவா!","explanation":"This poem belongs to the Potuviyal tiṇai and the theme of Kaiyaṟunilai, which expresses a state of helplessness and grief upon the death of a patron. The poet Pottiyar laments the death of his beloved friend and patron, the Chola king Koperuncolan (referred to as Killi). He compares his own sorrow upon seeing the empty assembly ground of the king's ancient town to the grief of a mahout who has lost his elephant. The mahout stands weeping before the empty tethering post in the bustling shed where the elephant once lived. This powerful image of desolation captures the poet's profound sense of loss and helplessness after the king's departure.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}